gtk: vmlab: a hidden window, shown and hidden on request

Every start of the VM now makes its real window, hidden when VMLAB_WINDOW_HIDDEN is set, so
`vm view` can show it later instead of opening a VNC viewer, which resized the guest and
broke an agent's clicks. VMLAB_WINDOW_CONTROL names a FIFO that QEMU reads lines from:
"show" presents the window (maximized first with VMLAB_WINDOW_MAXIMIZE), "hide" hides it.
QEMU opens it read-write so it never sees end-of-file when a writer closes.
VMLAB_WINDOW_STATE_FILE gets "shown" or "hidden" after each change, so `vm` can tell.

With the FIFO, the title bar has a hide button left of full screen: the window goes and
the VM keeps running. Close still shuts the VM down. The Mac window has the same button
(../../reims/libdecor-vmlab/vmlab-titlebar.patch).

A hidden window shares no clipboard: the guest cannot read the host's clipboard, or set
it, while nobody is looking at the VM.

The full screen button and the hide button come from one maker, so both look alike.
